From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 11:33:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(hud): acknowledge Bedrock boss bar registration

The Bedrock client replies to each boss bar Add and Remove with a
serverbound BossEvent of type PlayerAdded or PlayerRemoved for the same
actor. ViaBedrock cancelled these events without a reply. Galaxite uses
the exchange as a load check when it switches a player into
BlasterWars: it sends Add then Remove for the local player's unique ID
about every 0.25 seconds, pins the player with MovePlayer corrections,
withholds the game items, and kicks with "could not finish loading"
after about 60 seconds.

Evidence, Bedrock 1.26.60 (protocol 2225), official client through the
StackAnvil recording relay on 2026-11-10: the client answered both the
hub probe and the BlasterWars probe within 30 ms, received the
Repeater within 23 seconds and stayed connected. Each reply copies the
actor ID, name, filtered name and percent from the request and carries
color BLUE (1) and overlay PROGRESS (0), although the request carried
PINK (0). The regression test replays those exact request and reply
bytes.

The reply is sent only for Add and Remove of an actor the translator
tracks. The captures cover requests that target the local player; the
same reply for other boss actors follows the documented update types
but has no native capture yet.
